1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,686
What's today's video about? It's a complete summary of N5 grammar!

2
00:00:07,308 --> 00:00:16,290
At some point in the video, a question will appear in Japanese. If you catch it, leave a comment!

3
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:19,718
Scene 1: Favorite Foods and Lunch Plans

4
00:00:19,718 --> 00:00:26,518
Suzuki, what’s your favorite Japanese food?

5
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:31,212
I love sushi the most.

6
00:00:31,236 --> 00:00:33,814
How about you, Tanaka?

7
00:00:33,837 --> 00:00:39,437
I prefer ramen over sushi.

8
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:43,678
I especially love soy sauce ramen.

9
00:00:43,701 --> 00:00:47,572
Soy sauce ramen is so good!

10
00:00:47,596 --> 00:00:51,962
I also like miso ramen.

11
00:00:51,985 --> 00:00:55,752
Miso ramen is great too!

12
00:00:55,775 --> 00:01:00,868
Suzuki, have you eaten lunch yet?

13
00:01:00,892 --> 00:01:04,825
No, not yet.

14
00:01:04,848 --> 00:01:08,288
Have you eaten yet, Tanaka?

15
00:01:08,312 --> 00:01:12,926
No, I haven’t either.

16
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:18,083
Then how about we go to the ramen shop near the station?

17
00:01:18,106 --> 00:01:20,377
Sounds good!

18
00:01:20,401 --> 00:01:23,834
Is that place famous?

19
00:01:23,857 --> 00:01:27,824
Yeah, it was featured on TV.

20
00:01:27,847 --> 00:01:32,580
I heard there’s always a long line.

21
00:01:32,603 --> 00:01:36,537
But there aren’t many people around lunchtime on weekdays.

22
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:40,365
We’ll probably get in right away.

23
00:01:40,388 --> 00:01:42,421
Really?

24
00:01:42,444 --> 00:01:45,678
Let’s go now then!

25
00:01:45,701 --> 00:01:48,834
I’ll drive us there.

26
00:01:48,857 --> 00:01:50,509
Thanks!

27
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:54,032
Are you a good driver, Tanaka?

28
00:01:54,055 --> 00:01:55,791
Yes, I am.

29
00:01:55,815 --> 00:02:00,782
I drive every day, so I’m pretty good.

30
00:02:00,805 --> 00:02:03,176
No worries.

31
00:02:03,199 --> 00:02:05,657
That’s reassuring.

32
00:02:05,681 --> 00:02:12,647
I don’t know how to drive at all, so I’m jealous!

33
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:16,037
Don’t you have a car, Suzuki?

34
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,426
No, I don’t.

35
00:02:19,449 --> 00:02:23,383
I always take the train or bus.

36
00:02:23,406 --> 00:02:29,039
Oh, I can see the ramen shop’s sign over there!

37
00:02:29,062 --> 00:02:31,197
You’re right!

38
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:34,994
Is that the place with the blue sign?

39
00:02:35,017 --> 00:02:38,184
Yes, that’s the one!

40
00:02:38,207 --> 00:02:42,340
There’s a parking lot in front of the shop.

41
00:02:42,363 --> 00:02:48,260
There aren’t many cars today, so we can park easily.

42
00:02:48,284 --> 00:02:50,250
Great!

43
00:02:50,273 --> 00:02:55,078
I’m starving—I want to eat a lot!

44
00:02:55,102 --> 00:02:59,944
Yeah, let’s order the big ramen!

45
00:02:59,967 --> 00:03:07,072
The link to the site for reviewing today’s video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

46
00:03:07,072 --> 00:03:10,072
Scene 2: How to Spend Your Day Off

47
00:03:10,072 --> 00:03:15,639
Suzuki, what do you like to do on your days off?

48
00:03:15,662 --> 00:03:20,795
I enjoy watching movies at home.

49
00:03:20,818 --> 00:03:23,290
How about you, Tanaka?

50
00:03:23,313 --> 00:03:29,157
I love traveling to Kyoto with friends.

51
00:03:29,181 --> 00:03:32,147
Kyoto is so interesting!

52
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:34,304
Kyoto, huh?

53
00:03:34,327 --> 00:03:36,093
Sounds good!

54
00:03:36,116 --> 00:03:41,367
Kyoto has so many ancient temples, doesn’t it?

55
00:03:41,391 --> 00:03:47,243
Have you ever been to Kyoto, Suzuki?

56
00:03:47,266 --> 00:03:52,717
No, I’ve never been.

57
00:03:52,741 --> 00:03:55,274
I’d love to go someday.

58
00:03:55,297 --> 00:03:59,387
Why don’t we go this upcoming break?

59
00:03:59,410 --> 00:04:02,977
It’s just a quick Shinkansen ride away.

60
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,414
The Shinkansen?

61
00:04:05,437 --> 00:04:10,370
How long does it take from Tokyo to Kyoto?

62
00:04:10,393 --> 00:04:13,560
About two and a half hours.

63
00:04:13,583 --> 00:04:15,949
That’s really fast.

64
00:04:15,972 --> 00:04:20,506
Two and a half hours? That *is* fast.

65
00:04:20,529 --> 00:04:24,866
But the Shinkansen is a bit pricey, isn’t it?

66
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:28,223
Yeah, it’s a little expensive.

67
00:04:28,246 --> 00:04:34,846
But it’s faster and more convenient than the highway bus.

68
00:04:34,868 --> 00:04:36,645
True.

69
00:04:36,669 --> 00:04:40,302
Where are you planning to stay in Kyoto?

70
00:04:40,325 --> 00:04:44,658
I always stay at traditional inns.

71
00:04:44,681 --> 00:04:48,448
The food at those inns is absolutely delicious.

72
00:04:48,471 --> 00:04:52,110
A traditional inn? Sounds wonderful.

73
00:04:52,134 --> 00:04:58,545
I love old Japanese buildings, so I’m really interested.

74
00:04:58,568 --> 00:05:02,801
There are beautiful gardens near the inn too.

75
00:05:02,824 --> 00:05:05,624
I’d love to see them.

76
00:05:05,647 --> 00:05:10,134
I’ve heard Kyoto’s autumn foliage is stunning.

77
00:05:10,158 --> 00:05:13,841
Yes, it’s breathtaking.

78
00:05:13,864 --> 00:05:20,197
But autumn is the busiest season, so booking can be tough.

79
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,238
Really?

80
00:05:22,262 --> 00:05:26,934
Then we should plan ahead.

81
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:29,691
Yes, let’s do that.

82
00:05:29,714 --> 00:05:34,647
I’ll look up some inn details tomorrow.

83
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:36,723
Thanks, I appreciate it.

84
00:05:36,747 --> 00:05:39,444
I’m really looking forward to it.

85
00:05:39,468 --> 00:05:49,150
Let me know if you could follow along in the comments!

86
00:05:49,150 --> 00:05:52,150
Scene 3: Introducing a New Bag

87
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:56,883
Suzuki, is that a new bag?

88
00:05:56,906 --> 00:05:59,839
Did you buy it yesterday?

89
00:05:59,862 --> 00:06:01,517
Yes, I am.

90
00:06:01,541 --> 00:06:06,559
I got this at a department store yesterday.

91
00:06:06,583 --> 00:06:09,186
It’s really nice!

92
00:06:09,209 --> 00:06:12,891
How much was it?

93
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:15,748
It was 20,000 yen.

94
00:06:15,771 --> 00:06:18,771
That was a bit pricey.

95
00:06:18,794 --> 00:06:21,074
20,000 yen?

96
00:06:21,097 --> 00:06:23,730
That *is* a little expensive.

97
00:06:23,753 --> 00:06:27,487
But it looks really lightweight.

98
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:32,514
Yeah, it’s super light and easy to use.

99
00:06:32,537 --> 00:06:36,104
It has tons of pockets inside.

100
00:06:36,127 --> 00:06:39,538
Bags with lots of pockets are so handy.

101
00:06:39,562 --> 00:06:43,095
I want a new bag too.

102
00:06:43,118 --> 00:06:47,006
What kind of bag are you looking for, Tanaka?

103
00:06:47,029 --> 00:06:49,429
For your commute?

104
00:06:49,452 --> 00:06:53,852
I need a bag for work.

105
00:06:53,875 --> 00:06:57,709
I'd like a bag big enough for my laptop.

106
00:06:57,732 --> 00:07:02,565
Why don't we go to the same department store together?

107
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:06,445
They have so many bag shops there.

108
00:07:06,468 --> 00:07:08,435
Sounds good!

109
00:07:08,458 --> 00:07:12,025
Where is that department store located?

110
00:07:12,048 --> 00:07:15,122
It's near Shinjuku Station.

111
00:07:15,145 --> 00:07:18,427
It's about a five-minute walk from the station.

112
00:07:18,451 --> 00:07:21,818
Shinjuku is close to the office, isn't it?

113
00:07:21,841 --> 00:07:25,140
I'm planning to go this weekend.

114
00:07:25,164 --> 00:07:32,434
There aren't many people on Saturday mornings, so shopping is easier.

115
00:07:32,457 --> 00:07:34,125
Got it.

116
00:07:34,148 --> 00:07:37,382
I'll go Saturday morning, then.

117
00:07:37,404 --> 00:07:40,571
Hope you find a great bag!

118
00:07:40,594 --> 00:07:42,245
Yes, I am.

119
00:07:42,269 --> 00:07:44,669
Oh, Suzuki-san.

120
00:07:44,692 --> 00:07:48,730
What's that bag next to your laptop case?

121
00:07:48,753 --> 00:07:53,519
This is a souvenir I got from a friend yesterday.

122
00:07:53,542 --> 00:07:56,676
It's some Hokkaido sweets.

123
00:07:56,699 --> 00:07:59,517
Hokkaido sweets?

124
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:01,216
Sounds good!

125
00:08:01,239 --> 00:08:05,172
Hokkaido is famous for its sweet treats.

126
00:08:05,195 --> 00:08:08,462
Would you like one?

127
00:08:08,485 --> 00:08:11,335
They're really delicious.

128
00:08:11,358 --> 00:08:12,958
Thanks!

129
00:08:12,982 --> 00:08:17,215
Sure, I'll have one with some hot tea.

130
00:08:17,238 --> 00:08:20,238
Scene 4: Weather Forecast and Tennis Cancellation

131
00:08:20,238 --> 00:08:25,474
Suzuki-san, did you check tomorrow's weather forecast?

132
00:08:25,497 --> 00:08:29,064
No, not yet.

133
00:08:29,088 --> 00:08:31,772
Is it going to be sunny tomorrow?

134
00:08:31,795 --> 00:08:36,995
No, they said it's going to rain heavily.

135
00:08:37,018 --> 00:08:39,885
And it'll be windy too.

136
00:08:39,908 --> 00:08:44,113
Heavy rain? That's too bad.

137
00:08:44,136 --> 00:08:48,603
I was planning to play tennis outside tomorrow.

138
00:08:48,626 --> 00:08:50,798
Tennis?

139
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:55,355
You shouldn't play tennis outside tomorrow.

140
00:08:55,378 --> 00:08:57,395
It's dangerous.

141
00:08:57,418 --> 00:08:59,152
True.

142
00:08:59,175 --> 00:09:03,264
I guess I'll cancel tomorrow's tennis, then.

143
00:09:03,288 --> 00:09:05,454
That's a shame.

144
00:09:05,477 --> 00:09:08,050
It's for the best.

145
00:09:08,073 --> 00:09:12,326
They also said the temperature will drop tomorrow.

146
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:14,194
It's going to get cold.

147
00:09:14,218 --> 00:09:16,837
It's going to get cold?

148
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:21,158
Then I should wear a warm coat.

149
00:09:21,182 --> 00:09:25,348
Yes, make sure you don't catch a cold.

150
00:09:25,371 --> 00:09:28,738
The weather's going to be bad tomorrow.

151
00:09:28,761 --> 00:09:34,420
Tanaka-san, do you have any plans to go out tomorrow?

152
00:09:34,444 --> 00:09:38,844
No, I'm not going anywhere.

153
00:09:38,867 --> 00:09:42,233
I'm planning to read at home.

154
00:09:42,256 --> 00:09:44,456
That sounds nice.

155
00:09:44,479 --> 00:09:50,013
I think I'll relax at home tomorrow too.

156
00:09:50,036 --> 00:09:53,902
What will you do at home, Suzuki-san?

157
00:09:53,925 --> 00:09:57,823
I'll study Japanese.

158
00:09:57,847 --> 00:10:03,267
I have a test next month, so I need to work hard.

159
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:06,296
You have a test coming up?

160
00:10:06,319 --> 00:10:08,594
That sounds tough.

161
00:10:08,617 --> 00:10:11,150
What kind of test is it?

162
00:10:11,173 --> 00:10:13,773
It's a kanji test.

163
00:10:13,796 --> 00:10:18,094
Learning kanji is really difficult.

164
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:22,161
You should practice writing kanji every day.

165
00:10:22,185 --> 00:10:25,385
I practiced every single day.

166
00:10:25,408 --> 00:10:29,903
Yes, I practice for an hour every day.

167
00:10:29,926 --> 00:10:33,609
But I keep forgetting them.

168
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:36,633
Everyone struggles with that at first.

169
00:10:36,656 --> 00:10:39,463
Don’t give up—keep at it!

170
00:10:39,487 --> 00:10:41,744
Yes, thank you so much.

171
00:10:41,767 --> 00:10:44,984
I’ll give it my all tomorrow!

172
00:10:45,008 --> 00:10:48,008
Scene 5: Booking a Haircut & Salon Skills

173
00:10:48,008 --> 00:10:54,894
Suzuki, do you have a moment? I’d like to ask you something.

174
00:10:54,917 --> 00:10:58,084
Sure, what is it?

175
00:10:58,107 --> 00:11:03,154
I’m free now, so go ahead.

176
00:11:03,178 --> 00:11:08,311
Where do you usually get your hair cut, Suzuki?

177
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:13,668
I go to the salon in front of the station.

178
00:11:13,692 --> 00:11:17,625
The one with the blue sign.

179
00:11:17,648 --> 00:11:21,181
Oh, that place?

180
00:11:21,204 --> 00:11:24,095
Are they good there?

181
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:28,418
Yes, they’re really skilled.

182
00:11:28,442 --> 00:11:32,058
Their cutting technique is amazing.

183
00:11:32,082 --> 00:11:35,250
And the staff are so friendly.

184
00:11:35,273 --> 00:11:38,440
How do you make a reservation?

185
00:11:38,463 --> 00:11:40,296
Do you call them?

186
00:11:40,319 --> 00:11:44,453
You can book online—it’s easier than calling.

187
00:11:44,476 --> 00:11:47,342
Much simpler than phoning.

188
00:11:47,365 --> 00:11:49,377
Really?

189
00:11:49,401 --> 00:11:53,419
I want to get my hair cut next week.

190
00:11:53,442 --> 00:11:57,209
It’s gotten too long.

191
00:11:57,233 --> 00:12:00,766
Yeah, it has grown out a bit.

192
00:12:00,789 --> 00:12:05,556
I think a shorter style would suit you, Tanaka.

193
00:12:05,579 --> 00:12:07,612
Thanks!

194
00:12:07,635 --> 00:12:12,002
How much does it cost there?

195
00:12:12,025 --> 00:12:15,802
A haircut is around 4,000 yen.

196
00:12:15,825 --> 00:12:19,510
I think it’s a bit cheaper than other salons.

197
00:12:19,534 --> 00:12:23,767
4,000 yen? That’s great.

198
00:12:23,790 --> 00:12:29,157
It’s not expensive, so I’ll book an appointment and go.

199
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:35,018
Saturdays get busy, so a weekday evening would be better.

200
00:12:35,041 --> 00:12:37,844
They’re open until 9 PM.

201
00:12:37,867 --> 00:12:42,364
Until 9 PM? That’s really convenient.

202
00:12:42,388 --> 00:12:45,521
I’ll book an appointment after work.

203
00:12:45,544 --> 00:12:48,744
Yes, do that.

204
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:52,574
That way, you can take your time.

205
00:12:52,598 --> 00:12:57,577
When are you going next, Suzuki?

206
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:03,445
I’m planning to get a perm at the end of next month.

207
00:13:03,468 --> 00:13:06,435
A perm? That’ll look great!

208
00:13:06,458 --> 00:13:09,791
You’ll look so stylish!

209
00:13:09,814 --> 00:13:11,948
Yes, thank you so much.

210
00:13:11,971 --> 00:13:14,771
I’m really looking forward to it.

211
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:17,794
Scene 6: Shopping & My New Camera

212
00:13:17,794 --> 00:13:23,560
Suzuki, did you go shopping anywhere yesterday?

213
00:13:23,583 --> 00:13:25,983
I saw you near the station.

214
00:13:26,006 --> 00:13:32,006
Yeah, I went to a big electronics store in Shibuya yesterday.

215
00:13:32,029 --> 00:13:34,429
What did you buy?

216
00:13:34,452 --> 00:13:37,427
A new appliance?

217
00:13:37,451 --> 00:13:40,726
I bought a new camera.

218
00:13:40,749 --> 00:13:42,983
Here it is.

219
00:13:43,006 --> 00:13:46,103
It's the latest model, just released yesterday.

220
00:13:46,126 --> 00:13:50,203
Wow, that's a sleek camera!

221
00:13:50,227 --> 00:13:52,460
That must've been expensive, right?

222
00:13:52,483 --> 00:13:55,970
Yeah, it was 50,000 yen.

223
00:13:55,994 --> 00:14:00,127
It was a bit pricey for me.

224
00:14:00,150 --> 00:14:02,487
50,000 yen?

225
00:14:02,511 --> 00:14:10,244
But you're great at taking photos, Suzuki. You need a good camera!

226
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:14,308
Oh no, I'm still not that good.

227
00:14:14,332 --> 00:14:17,532
I want to practice more.

228
00:14:17,555 --> 00:14:21,688
What kind of photos do you plan to take with this camera?

229
00:14:21,711 --> 00:14:28,244
I want to capture beautiful scenery in Japan and photos of delicious food.

230
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:29,801
Sounds good!

231
00:14:29,824 --> 00:14:34,990
Next time, take a photo of the food I cook, okay?

232
00:14:35,013 --> 00:14:38,747
Sure, I'd love to!

233
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:43,053
Your cooking always looks so delicious.

234
00:14:43,076 --> 00:14:45,276
Thanks!

235
00:14:45,299 --> 00:14:47,387
That makes me happy!

236
00:14:47,410 --> 00:14:50,977
Getting compliments like that gives me confidence.

237
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,495
Do you have a camera, Tanaka?

238
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:58,355
No, I don’t.

239
00:14:58,378 --> 00:15:01,995
I always take photos with my smartphone.

240
00:15:02,018 --> 00:15:08,913
These days, smartphones take really clear photos, so they're good enough.

241
00:15:08,937 --> 00:15:15,903
Yeah, but seeing your new camera makes me want one too.

242
00:15:15,926 --> 00:15:20,260
How about we go to the electronics store together sometime?

243
00:15:20,283 --> 00:15:23,249
There are so many cameras to check out.

244
00:15:23,272 --> 00:15:24,963
Sounds good!

245
00:15:24,987 --> 00:15:27,987
Just looking around sounds fun.

246
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:34,210
Yeah, and there are events this weekend, so it’ll be even more exciting!

247
00:15:34,233 --> 00:15:36,566
Sounds good, let’s go!

248
00:15:36,589 --> 00:15:39,589
Scene 7: Overtime and Planning for Rest / Balancing Work and Relaxation

249
00:15:39,589 --> 00:15:43,795
Suzuki, have you been busy lately?

250
00:15:43,819 --> 00:15:47,586
You look a little tired.

251
00:15:47,609 --> 00:15:54,375
Yeah, this week’s been really hectic with work.

252
00:15:54,398 --> 00:15:58,432
What time do you finish work every day?

253
00:15:58,455 --> 00:16:02,899
I’ve been working until 8 PM every day.

254
00:16:02,922 --> 00:16:05,855
Yesterday, I worked until 8 PM too.

255
00:16:05,878 --> 00:16:08,932
That must be exhausting.

256
00:16:08,955 --> 00:16:15,632
Working overtime every day isn’t good for you. Don’t push yourself too hard.

257
00:16:15,656 --> 00:16:17,456
Thanks!

258
00:16:17,479 --> 00:16:23,212
But I think things will calm down after this project ends next week.

259
00:16:23,235 --> 00:16:26,469
Oh, that’s great!

260
00:16:26,492 --> 00:16:30,225
What do you want to do when you have free time?

261
00:16:30,248 --> 00:16:34,067
I’m planning to go to the beach with friends.

262
00:16:34,091 --> 00:16:39,372
I want to swim and eat some fresh seafood.

263
00:16:39,396 --> 00:16:42,642
The beach? That sounds nice!

264
00:16:42,665 --> 00:16:45,914
Which beach are you going to?

265
00:16:45,938 --> 00:16:49,904
We’re going to a beach in Kanagawa.

266
00:16:49,927 --> 00:16:54,201
It’s only about an hour from Tokyo by train.

267
00:16:54,225 --> 00:16:58,032
An hour? That’s pretty close!

268
00:16:58,056 --> 00:17:01,262
I love the ocean too.

269
00:17:01,286 --> 00:17:04,154
The sandy beaches are so beautiful.

270
00:17:04,177 --> 00:17:07,449
Would you like to join us too, Tanaka-san?

271
00:17:07,472 --> 00:17:10,513
Our friends would be thrilled!

272
00:17:10,537 --> 00:17:12,829
Are you sure? That’d be great!

273
00:17:12,853 --> 00:17:15,786
I’d love to come with you!

274
00:17:15,809 --> 00:17:18,548
The ocean is so much fun.

275
00:17:18,572 --> 00:17:23,669
Let’s go next Saturday!

276
00:17:23,693 --> 00:17:28,329
It’ll be more convenient if we go by car, so I’ll rent one.

277
00:17:28,353 --> 00:17:30,319
Got it.

278
00:17:30,342 --> 00:17:34,675
I’ll cover the rental car cost.

279
00:17:34,698 --> 00:17:38,133
No, let’s split it evenly.

280
00:17:38,157 --> 00:17:41,566
That’s fair—sounds good to me!

281
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,590
Really?

282
00:17:43,613 --> 00:17:48,792
I’ll make breakfast and bring it along for the day.

283
00:17:48,815 --> 00:17:51,581
A packed lunch!

284
00:17:51,604 --> 00:17:54,302
Wow, thank you so much!

285
00:17:54,326 --> 00:17:59,774
I’m really looking forward to your homemade lunch—it’s always delicious!

286
00:17:59,797 --> 00:18:02,830
Leave it to me!

287
00:18:02,853 --> 00:18:04,987
I’ll make plenty.

288
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:08,543
Yeah, it’ll definitely be sunny!

289
00:18:08,566 --> 00:18:11,566
Scene 8: Party Prep and Shopping

290
00:18:11,566 --> 00:18:17,499
Fuzuki-san, have you finished preparing for tomorrow’s party yet?

291
00:18:17,522 --> 00:18:21,166
No, not yet.

292
00:18:21,190 --> 00:18:25,797
There’s so much to buy, so I’m heading out to shop now.

293
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:28,153
What are you going to get?

294
00:18:28,176 --> 00:18:29,980
At the supermarket?

295
00:18:30,004 --> 00:18:34,206
I plan to buy lots of drinks and snacks.

296
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,663
We’ll need a ton of them.

297
00:18:36,686 --> 00:18:42,023
It’ll be heavy, so I’ll come with you and drive.

298
00:18:42,046 --> 00:18:44,114
I’ll handle the driving.

299
00:18:44,137 --> 00:18:45,775
Thanks!

300
00:18:45,799 --> 00:18:47,698
That’d be a huge help!

301
00:18:47,721 --> 00:18:50,521
It would’ve been tough to do alone.

302
00:18:50,544 --> 00:18:53,950
How many people are coming to the party?

303
00:18:53,973 --> 00:18:57,573
Around twenty people are expected.

304
00:18:57,596 --> 00:19:00,263
It’s going to be so lively!

305
00:19:00,286 --> 00:19:05,086
Twenty people? That’s a big party!

306
00:19:05,109 --> 00:19:07,312
Where’s the venue?

307
00:19:07,335 --> 00:19:10,618
It’s a rental space near the office.

308
00:19:10,642 --> 00:19:13,609
That place is spacious and clean.

309
00:19:13,632 --> 00:19:16,001
Oh, that place?

310
00:19:16,025 --> 00:19:20,858
It’s a new building, so it’s a great spot.

311
00:19:20,881 --> 00:19:26,448
Yeah, but we have to take all the trash home.

312
00:19:26,471 --> 00:19:28,604
They’re strict about that.

313
00:19:28,627 --> 00:19:32,960
Really? That’ll be a bit tough.

314
00:19:32,983 --> 00:19:36,950
We’ll need a lot of big trash bags.

315
00:19:36,973 --> 00:19:42,706
Right, I’ll grab some today at the supermarket next to the electronics store.

316
00:19:42,729 --> 00:19:46,008
What time does the party start?

317
00:19:46,032 --> 00:19:48,904
It starts at 7 PM.

318
00:19:48,927 --> 00:19:50,861
And ends at 9 PM.

319
00:19:50,884 --> 00:19:52,617
So, two hours.

320
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:55,044
Got it.

321
00:19:55,067 --> 00:19:59,701
Suzuki-san, what time will you head to the venue tomorrow?

322
00:19:59,724 --> 00:20:03,900
I'll head over at five since I have some preparations to do.

323
00:20:03,923 --> 00:20:08,381
Then I'll come at five too and help you get ready.

324
00:20:08,404 --> 00:20:10,337
Thanks!

325
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:13,894
Mr. Tanaka, you're so kind!

326
00:20:13,916 --> 00:20:16,207
You're always such a big help.

327
00:20:16,231 --> 00:20:21,877
Oh no, I just love parties and want to have fun!

328
00:20:21,901 --> 00:20:24,572
Haha, I see.

329
00:20:24,595 --> 00:20:28,676
Let's make this a fantastic party together!

330
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:31,700
Scene 9: Mastering Japanese / Tips for Improving Your Japanese Skills

331
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:36,597
Suzuki, how's life in Japan treating you?

332
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:42,105
It's been a year already, so I've gotten used to it.

333
00:20:42,128 --> 00:20:45,395
Life here is really convenient.

334
00:20:45,418 --> 00:20:49,651
Your Japanese has improved so much!

335
00:20:49,674 --> 00:20:52,282
Your pronunciation is really clear.

336
00:20:52,305 --> 00:20:56,105
Oh no, I still have a long way to go.

337
00:20:56,128 --> 00:21:00,162
I don't understand news Japanese at all.

338
00:21:00,185 --> 00:21:05,751
News Japanese has a lot of difficult vocabulary.

339
00:21:05,774 --> 00:21:10,646
You should watch TV every day.

340
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:13,303
I do watch it every day.

341
00:21:13,326 --> 00:21:19,060
But the news anchors speak way too fast.

342
00:21:19,083 --> 00:21:20,816
True.

343
00:21:20,839 --> 00:21:26,972
Maybe you should start with simple anime for kids.

344
00:21:26,995 --> 00:21:29,806
Anime for kids?

345
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,722
That's a great idea!

346
00:21:32,745 --> 00:21:35,618
The language is much simpler.

347
00:21:35,642 --> 00:21:44,479
Yeah, Japanese kids learn language by watching anime—it's really effective.

348
00:21:44,502 --> 00:21:45,937
Got it.

349
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:49,327
I'll start watching it right away from today!

350
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:54,317
What's the hardest part about living in Japan?

351
00:21:54,341 --> 00:21:56,560
Is it the cost of living?

352
00:21:56,583 --> 00:22:02,230
No, it's the packed trains every morning.

353
00:22:02,254 --> 00:22:06,587
Morning rush-hour trains are brutal.

354
00:22:06,610 --> 00:22:10,864
Ah, the packed trains.

355
00:22:10,888 --> 00:22:15,534
No one in Japan likes those.

356
00:22:15,558 --> 00:22:18,158
They're so cramped and uncomfortable.

357
00:22:18,181 --> 00:22:23,275
Do you take those packed trains every morning, Tanaka?

358
00:22:23,299 --> 00:22:30,499
No, I hate trains, so I always bike to work.

359
00:22:30,523 --> 00:22:32,726
That's healthy!

360
00:22:32,749 --> 00:22:34,986
You bike?

361
00:22:35,010 --> 00:22:37,987
What do you do on rainy days?

362
00:22:38,011 --> 00:22:39,944
That must be tough.

363
00:22:39,967 --> 00:22:43,367
On rainy days, I take the bus.

364
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:48,447
Buses are less crowded than trains, so they're quieter.

365
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:50,237
Really?

366
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:54,098
Less stress from trains sounds great.

367
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:58,170
I think I'll start taking the bus from tomorrow.

368
00:22:58,193 --> 00:23:01,659
Yeah, give it a try.

369
00:23:01,682 --> 00:23:05,492
I think you'll find it much more comfortable than the train.

370
00:23:05,516 --> 00:23:07,449
Got it.

371
00:23:07,472 --> 00:23:11,210
Thanks for all the great tips!

372
00:23:11,234 --> 00:23:14,234
Scene 10: A Hidden Gem / Discovering a New Café

373
00:23:14,234 --> 00:23:20,100
Suzuki, were you at that new café near the station yesterday?

374
00:23:20,123 --> 00:23:22,923
Yeah, I was there.

375
00:23:22,946 --> 00:23:26,029
I was having coffee around three.

376
00:23:26,052 --> 00:23:28,419
How did you know that?

377
00:23:28,442 --> 00:23:31,413
So it *was* you, Suzuki!

378
00:23:31,436 --> 00:23:34,207
I should’ve said hi.

379
00:23:34,231 --> 00:23:37,831
Oh, Tanaka, were you at that café too?

380
00:23:37,854 --> 00:23:42,220
No, I just drove by.

381
00:23:42,243 --> 00:23:46,010
I saw you near the window.

382
00:23:46,033 --> 00:23:48,400
Ah, I see.

383
00:23:48,423 --> 00:23:53,681
That café’s so quiet—I go there all the time to study.

384
00:23:53,704 --> 00:23:56,974
Is their coffee any good?

385
00:23:56,997 --> 00:24:00,531
Oh, it’s *amazing*.

386
00:24:00,554 --> 00:24:03,087
The aroma is just incredible.

387
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:06,317
They’ve got a great selection of teas too.

388
00:24:06,341 --> 00:24:07,987
Sounds good!

389
00:24:08,010 --> 00:24:12,882
It’s such a stylish place—I’ve been meaning to check it out.

390
00:24:12,906 --> 00:24:17,239
Why don’t we go together after work today?

391
00:24:17,262 --> 00:24:19,146
Today?

392
00:24:19,169 --> 00:24:26,336
I get off at five, so I can make it. Same here!

393
00:24:26,359 --> 00:24:30,092
Work hasn’t been too crazy this week, so—

394
00:24:30,115 --> 00:24:32,574
Then let’s go!

395
00:24:32,598 --> 00:24:36,271
Do they have any sweet cakes?

396
00:24:36,294 --> 00:24:40,861
Yeah, they’ve got chocolate cake and Swiss rolls.

397
00:24:40,884 --> 00:24:43,550
Super rich and delicious.

398
00:24:43,573 --> 00:24:47,973
Ooh, I *love* chocolate cake!

399
00:24:47,996 --> 00:24:50,689
Sweets are my weakness.

400
00:24:50,712 --> 00:24:55,567
Their chocolate cake is the most popular item.

401
00:24:55,591 --> 00:24:58,958
It sells out fast, though.

402
00:24:58,981 --> 00:25:00,395
Really?

403
00:25:00,418 --> 00:25:04,673
We’d better hurry before it’s gone!

404
00:25:04,697 --> 00:25:10,133
No worries—we can be there by 5:30.

405
00:25:10,156 --> 00:25:11,994
I’m so excited!

406
00:25:12,017 --> 00:25:15,952
Guess I’ll wrap up work early today.

407
00:25:15,976 --> 00:25:19,066
Yeah, let’s power through!

408
00:25:19,090 --> 00:25:22,090
Scene 11: Shopping Plans

409
00:25:22,090 --> 00:25:27,904
The weather’s nice—wanna go somewhere?

410
00:25:27,928 --> 00:25:31,405
I’m looking for a new bag.

411
00:25:31,429 --> 00:25:33,995
Where are you thinking of going?

412
00:25:34,018 --> 00:25:38,088
The department store by the station.

413
00:25:38,112 --> 00:25:41,112
What kind of bag are you looking for?

414
00:25:41,135 --> 00:25:45,611
Something big.

415
00:25:45,635 --> 00:25:49,612
What are you planning to put in it?

416
00:25:49,635 --> 00:25:54,002
A bunch of dictionaries and textbooks.

417
00:25:54,025 --> 00:25:56,392
That sounds heavy!

418
00:25:56,415 --> 00:26:02,948
Exactly—so I need something sturdy. What color do you want?

419
00:26:02,971 --> 00:26:07,045
Black would be perfect.

420
00:26:07,068 --> 00:26:10,468
Black bags look so sleek.

421
00:26:10,491 --> 00:26:14,558
I’d love to use it for school every day.

422
00:26:14,581 --> 00:26:18,548
There’s a shoe store in the department store too, you know.

423
00:26:18,571 --> 00:26:21,908
Oh, I’ve been wanting new shoes!

424
00:26:21,932 --> 00:26:24,581
What kind are you looking for?

425
00:26:24,605 --> 00:26:28,689
Something lightweight.

426
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:31,330
Great for walks!

427
00:26:31,354 --> 00:26:35,321
I want to walk more every day.

428
00:26:35,344 --> 00:26:40,782
Then let’s check out shoes at the department store today too!

429
00:26:40,805 --> 00:26:44,649
I'm really looking forward to today's shopping!

430
00:26:44,673 --> 00:26:49,406
I want to buy some delicious snacks at the department store.

431
00:26:49,429 --> 00:26:52,908
Let's eat them together after shopping.

432
00:26:52,931 --> 00:26:55,665
Let's head to the station now.

433
00:26:55,688 --> 00:26:58,688
Scene 12: Preparing for the Party and Cleaning Up

434
00:26:58,688 --> 00:27:02,578
I'm getting ready for tomorrow's party.

435
00:27:02,601 --> 00:27:06,606
I'm cleaning the room right now.

436
00:27:06,630 --> 00:27:08,278
Thanks!

437
00:27:08,301 --> 00:27:11,434
I've finished cleaning!

438
00:27:11,457 --> 00:27:14,691
What should we do next?

439
00:27:14,714 --> 00:27:18,853
Please set the food out on the table.

440
00:27:18,876 --> 00:27:21,757
Can I arrange them here?

441
00:27:21,781 --> 00:27:23,423
Sure, go ahead.

442
00:27:23,446 --> 00:27:26,823
Where are the drinks?

443
00:27:26,847 --> 00:27:29,780
They're in the fridge.

444
00:27:29,803 --> 00:27:32,644
Who's coming to the party?

445
00:27:32,667 --> 00:27:36,671
Ten of my classmates are coming.

446
00:27:36,695 --> 00:27:39,183
It's going to be so lively!

447
00:27:39,206 --> 00:27:42,944
That's why we should keep the windows open.

448
00:27:42,968 --> 00:27:45,866
Can I put on some music?

449
00:27:45,890 --> 00:27:49,657
Let's prepare while listening to music.

450
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:53,913
I have a new CD.

451
00:27:53,936 --> 00:27:56,582
Please play it.

452
00:27:56,606 --> 00:27:59,101
We don't have enough chairs, do we?

453
00:27:59,125 --> 00:28:02,691
Should I bring some from the next room?

454
00:28:02,714 --> 00:28:05,133
Please bring five.

455
00:28:05,157 --> 00:28:09,690
I'm making a lot of food, so please help me.

456
00:28:09,713 --> 00:28:13,580
I'm carrying them now.

457
00:28:13,603 --> 00:28:16,214
Please set the plates out too.

458
00:28:16,237 --> 00:28:18,604
Where are they?

459
00:28:18,627 --> 00:28:22,194
They're in the cupboard. Please take them out.

460
00:28:22,217 --> 00:28:24,819
I'm taking them out now.

461
00:28:24,842 --> 00:28:27,780
Please wash the glasses too.

462
00:28:27,803 --> 00:28:31,022
I've already washed the glasses.

463
00:28:31,046 --> 00:28:33,459
Thanks!

464
00:28:33,482 --> 00:28:36,482
Scene 13: Part-Time Job and Japanese Practice

465
00:28:36,482 --> 00:28:40,215
How's your new part-time job?

466
00:28:40,238 --> 00:28:44,238
I'm having so much fun every day!

467
00:28:44,261 --> 00:28:47,355
What kind of work do you do?

468
00:28:47,379 --> 00:28:51,512
I carry food at a restaurant.

469
00:28:51,535 --> 00:28:55,205
What time do you go in every day?

470
00:28:55,228 --> 00:28:59,028
I go in at 10 in the morning.

471
00:28:59,051 --> 00:29:05,289
When I arrive at the restaurant, I wash my hands and change clothes.

472
00:29:05,312 --> 00:29:07,797
Are the rules strict?

473
00:29:07,821 --> 00:29:12,621
We're not allowed to use our phones while working.

474
00:29:12,644 --> 00:29:15,500
Do you have to stand all the time?

475
00:29:15,524 --> 00:29:19,990
We can't sit in front of customers.

476
00:29:20,013 --> 00:29:22,346
That sounds tough.

477
00:29:22,369 --> 00:29:28,736
But I get to speak Japanese every day, so I'm improving!

478
00:29:28,759 --> 00:29:31,292
That's a great habit.

479
00:29:31,315 --> 00:29:36,715
I work here for three hours every day.

480
00:29:36,738 --> 00:29:40,548
Do you also cook?

481
00:29:40,572 --> 00:29:44,623
You don’t cook here.

482
00:29:44,647 --> 00:29:46,826
Just deliver the food?

483
00:29:46,850 --> 00:29:51,519
I deliver the food and then wash the dishes.

484
00:29:51,542 --> 00:29:53,879
Are you busy?

485
00:29:53,903 --> 00:29:58,436
Lunchtime is always hectic.

486
00:29:58,459 --> 00:30:01,626
Do you wash your own uniforms?

487
00:30:01,649 --> 00:30:04,482
The company takes care of the laundry.

488
00:30:04,505 --> 00:30:06,838
This is a great place to work!

489
00:30:06,861 --> 00:30:12,234
I’ve been working at this restaurant for a long time.

490
00:30:12,258 --> 00:30:15,258
Scene 14: Explaining a Travel Itinerary

491
00:30:15,258 --> 00:30:18,991
Let me walk you through today’s travel schedule.

492
00:30:19,014 --> 00:30:20,581
Sure, go ahead.

493
00:30:20,604 --> 00:30:25,379
We’ll leave the hotel at 8 AM and walk to the station.

494
00:30:25,402 --> 00:30:29,075
What do we do after we get to the station?

495
00:30:29,099 --> 00:30:34,366
We’ll buy tickets and then board the train.

496
00:30:34,390 --> 00:30:38,157
Will we eat on the train?

497
00:30:38,180 --> 00:30:42,113
We’ll have lunch after we arrive at the temple.

498
00:30:42,136 --> 00:30:44,303
What kind of temple is it?

499
00:30:44,326 --> 00:30:49,263
That temple has a spacious and beautiful garden.

500
00:30:49,287 --> 00:30:51,495
I’m so excited!

501
00:30:51,518 --> 00:30:57,012
The famous building there has a grand and impressive gate.

502
00:30:57,035 --> 00:30:59,835
I want to take lots of photos!

503
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:04,058
After visiting the temple, we’ll head to the nearby beach.

504
00:31:04,081 --> 00:31:07,419
What will we do at the beach?

505
00:31:07,443 --> 00:31:13,114
We’ll take a walk by the sea and then enjoy some fresh, delicious fish.

506
00:31:13,138 --> 00:31:17,350
That town is famous for its fresh and tasty seafood, isn’t it?

507
00:31:17,373 --> 00:31:22,339
After eating, we’ll buy some souvenirs.

508
00:31:22,362 --> 00:31:27,211
Will we head back to the hotel after buying souvenirs?

509
00:31:27,235 --> 00:31:30,689
We’ll return to the hotel by 7 PM.

510
00:31:30,713 --> 00:31:33,403
That’s a packed schedule!

511
00:31:33,426 --> 00:31:38,992
But the town is so scenic and fun to explore.

512
00:31:39,015 --> 00:31:42,470
I’ll take plenty of photos tomorrow!

513
00:31:42,494 --> 00:31:47,832
Let’s turn in early tonight so we can walk a lot tomorrow.

514
00:31:47,855 --> 00:31:50,422
I’ll go to bed early tonight.

515
00:31:50,445 --> 00:31:53,445
Scene 15: How to Respond When You're Sick

516
00:31:53,445 --> 00:31:55,902
What’s wrong?

517
00:31:55,926 --> 00:32:00,726
I have a slight headache and a fever.

518
00:32:00,749 --> 00:32:04,041
You must feel so sluggish.

519
00:32:04,064 --> 00:32:06,630
It really hurts.

520
00:32:06,653 --> 00:32:09,269
Have you been to the doctor yet?

521
00:32:09,293 --> 00:32:11,940
Not yet.

522
00:32:11,963 --> 00:32:15,702
There’s a good clinic nearby.

523
00:32:15,726 --> 00:32:19,341
Are the doctors there kind?

524
00:32:19,365 --> 00:32:22,098
You should go to the clinic.

525
00:32:22,121 --> 00:32:24,008
Got it.

526
00:32:24,032 --> 00:32:27,720
Don’t take a bath today.

527
00:32:27,743 --> 00:32:30,877
And no showers either.

528
00:32:30,900 --> 00:32:34,678
You need to get to bed early tonight.

529
00:32:34,701 --> 00:32:37,556
What should I eat?

530
00:32:37,580 --> 00:32:40,716
I’ll make some soft udon noodles for you.

531
00:32:40,739 --> 00:32:42,506
Sure, go ahead.

532
00:32:42,529 --> 00:32:47,103
I need to go grocery shopping now.

533
00:32:47,126 --> 00:32:50,816
I’ll wait in the room then.

534
00:32:50,839 --> 00:32:53,909
Take your medicine and then get some rest.

535
00:32:53,932 --> 00:32:55,511
Thanks!

536
00:32:55,535 --> 00:32:59,668
Do I have to submit my homework today?

537
00:32:59,691 --> 00:33:02,658
You don’t have to submit it today.

538
00:33:02,681 --> 00:33:06,490
You must bring it to school tomorrow.

539
00:33:06,514 --> 00:33:08,847
Got it.

540
00:33:08,870 --> 00:33:13,003
Lock the door and make sure no one can get in.

541
00:33:13,026 --> 00:33:14,467
I will.

542
00:33:14,491 --> 00:33:17,491
Scene 16: How to Spend Your Day Off

543
00:33:17,491 --> 00:33:20,785
Tomorrow’s a day off, isn’t it?

544
00:33:20,809 --> 00:33:24,409
No need to go to work tomorrow.

545
00:33:24,432 --> 00:33:26,832
That’s great!

546
00:33:26,855 --> 00:33:31,222
So I’ll stay up late tonight.

547
00:33:31,245 --> 00:33:34,245
What are you going to do tomorrow?

548
00:33:34,268 --> 00:33:37,868
I’m going out to take photos.

549
00:33:37,891 --> 00:33:40,224
Photos?

550
00:33:40,247 --> 00:33:45,936
My hobby is taking pictures of old buildings.

551
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:48,160
That’s wonderful!

552
00:33:48,183 --> 00:33:51,316
What’s your hobby?

553
00:33:51,339 --> 00:33:56,037
I love swimming.

554
00:33:56,061 --> 00:33:58,095
Do you go to the pool?

555
00:33:58,118 --> 00:34:01,085
I swim for two hours every day.

556
00:34:01,108 --> 00:34:03,351
That’s amazing!

557
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:07,553
I’m not into swimming at all.

558
00:34:07,577 --> 00:34:11,667
It’s fun, so I’ll teach you sometime.

559
00:34:11,690 --> 00:34:13,357
Sure, go ahead.

560
00:34:13,380 --> 00:34:17,834
What do you usually do before playing sports?

561
00:34:17,858 --> 00:34:22,824
I drink plenty of water before running.

562
00:34:22,847 --> 00:34:25,114
That’s important.

563
00:34:25,137 --> 00:34:31,871
Before swimming, I always do a little dance.

564
00:34:31,894 --> 00:34:33,863
Dance?

565
00:34:33,886 --> 00:34:36,257
That’s interesting!

566
00:34:36,281 --> 00:34:40,556
It warms up my body, so it’s great.

567
00:34:40,579 --> 00:34:44,779
I’ll get my camera ready before heading out.

568
00:34:44,802 --> 00:34:50,136
You don’t have to wake up early tomorrow, so get plenty of sleep.

569
00:34:50,159 --> 00:34:52,230
I will.

570
00:34:52,253 --> 00:34:55,253
Scene 17: Memories and Plans for a Trip to Japan

571
00:34:55,253 --> 00:34:59,871
Have you ever been to Japan?

572
00:34:59,895 --> 00:35:04,428
I went once last winter.

573
00:35:04,451 --> 00:35:06,622
Where did you go?

574
00:35:06,645 --> 00:35:09,478
I went to Hokkaido.

575
00:35:09,501 --> 00:35:12,997
What did you do in Hokkaido?

576
00:35:13,021 --> 00:35:17,988
I went skiing and ate delicious seafood.

577
00:35:18,011 --> 00:35:21,228
Do you know how to ski?

578
00:35:21,252 --> 00:35:26,452
I’ve been skiing since I was a child.

579
00:35:26,475 --> 00:35:30,075
I’ve never skied before.

580
00:35:30,098 --> 00:35:35,437
It’s not that hard, so let’s go together next time!

581
00:35:35,460 --> 00:35:38,993
Are you going to Japan again this summer?

582
00:35:39,016 --> 00:35:43,216
This summer, I want to visit Tokyo.

583
00:35:43,239 --> 00:35:45,873
What do you want to do in Tokyo?

584
00:35:45,895 --> 00:35:50,784
I’d like to visit old temples and go shopping.

585
00:35:50,808 --> 00:35:54,616
Have you ever been to the temples in Asakusa?

586
00:35:54,639 --> 00:35:57,173
Not yet.

587
00:35:57,196 --> 00:36:02,277
I went to Asakusa three years ago.

588
00:36:02,300 --> 00:36:05,067
Is it lively over there?

589
00:36:05,090 --> 00:36:09,857
I took photos and bought some souvenirs.

590
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:12,482
That’s interesting!

591
00:36:12,505 --> 00:36:18,871
Enjoy delicious food and beautiful sights in Tokyo!

592
00:36:18,894 --> 00:36:21,928
I want to travel a lot.

593
00:36:21,951 --> 00:36:24,951
Scene 18: Progress in Japanese Learning

594
00:36:24,951 --> 00:36:30,151
You've been studying Japanese for a long time, haven't you?

595
00:36:30,174 --> 00:36:33,707
I've been studying for two years now.

596
00:36:33,730 --> 00:36:38,063
Your conversation skills have really improved!

597
00:36:38,086 --> 00:36:39,962
Thanks!

598
00:36:39,986 --> 00:36:44,440
But kanji is still tough for me.

599
00:36:44,464 --> 00:36:48,443
How long do you study every day?

600
00:36:48,466 --> 00:36:53,033
I study for an hour every day.

601
00:36:53,056 --> 00:36:55,623
That's wonderful!

602
00:36:55,646 --> 00:37:00,730
I think next year will be even more challenging.

603
00:37:00,753 --> 00:37:04,720
But I'm sure you'll do just fine.

604
00:37:04,743 --> 00:37:07,876
I'll keep working hard every day.

605
00:37:07,899 --> 00:37:12,032
Do you want to work in Japan in the future?

606
00:37:12,055 --> 00:37:16,589
I'd like to work for a Japanese company.

607
00:37:16,612 --> 00:37:19,545
What kind of job do you want to do?

608
00:37:19,568 --> 00:37:23,419
I want to work with computers.

609
00:37:23,442 --> 00:37:27,331
I think you'll enjoy life in Japan.

610
00:37:27,354 --> 00:37:31,721
I'm a little worried because the cost of living is high.

611
00:37:31,744 --> 00:37:37,677
Tokyo is expensive, but other cities are more affordable.

612
00:37:37,700 --> 00:37:40,756
That makes me feel better.

613
00:37:40,780 --> 00:37:45,651
I think your Japanese will keep getting better.

614
00:37:45,674 --> 00:37:47,318
Thanks!

615
00:37:47,342 --> 00:37:50,475
It must be tough every day.

616
00:37:50,498 --> 00:37:53,969
Studying kanji has even become fun for me now.

617
00:37:53,993 --> 00:37:57,801
Let's keep working hard together!

618
00:37:57,824 --> 00:38:00,824
Scene 19: Confirming Time and Directions

619
00:38:00,824 --> 00:38:05,791
What time is Tanaka coming today?

620
00:38:05,814 --> 00:38:10,429
He said he'd be here at ten.

621
00:38:10,452 --> 00:38:14,419
It's already ten thirty!

622
00:38:14,442 --> 00:38:16,842
He's late.

623
00:38:16,865 --> 00:38:20,631
Maybe the roads are busy.

624
00:38:20,654 --> 00:38:23,929
Did he say he was coming by train?

625
00:38:23,953 --> 00:38:27,153
He said he was driving.

626
00:38:27,176 --> 00:38:31,310
The roads get busy when it rains.

627
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:36,466
If you go straight down this road, you'll come out in front of the station.

628
00:38:36,489 --> 00:38:41,531
If you turn at that corner, there's a narrow street, right?

629
00:38:41,555 --> 00:38:47,034
When no cars are passing, that street is really quiet.

630
00:38:47,057 --> 00:38:51,591
Does Tanaka know that street?

631
00:38:51,614 --> 00:38:54,385
He said he doesn't.

632
00:38:54,408 --> 00:38:57,475
Let me give him a call.

633
00:38:57,498 --> 00:38:59,670
Please do.

634
00:38:59,693 --> 00:39:03,460
Hello, is this Tanaka?

635
00:39:03,483 --> 00:39:06,852
Where are you now?

636
00:39:06,875 --> 00:39:11,209
He said he's in front of the station now.

637
00:39:11,232 --> 00:39:15,246
He'll be here in five minutes.

638
00:39:15,269 --> 00:39:19,436
He said he'll park his car in the nearby parking lot.

639
00:39:19,459 --> 00:39:24,925
Press this button, and the parking lot door will open.

640
00:39:24,948 --> 00:39:28,982
Let's open the door when Tanaka arrives.

641
00:39:29,005 --> 00:39:33,292
Let's wait here, then.

642
00:39:33,315 --> 00:39:36,315
Scene 20: Gifts and Cooking

643
00:39:36,315 --> 00:39:40,494
That watch is so beautiful.

644
00:39:40,518 --> 00:39:42,252
Thanks!

645
00:39:42,275 --> 00:39:46,548
My sister gave it to me for my birthday.

646
00:39:46,571 --> 00:39:49,844
She's such a kind sister.

647
00:39:49,868 --> 00:39:54,201
I gave her a scarf in return.

648
00:39:54,224 --> 00:39:57,757
Was she happy about it?

649
00:39:57,780 --> 00:40:00,597
She was really happy.

650
00:40:00,621 --> 00:40:04,755
You're such a great cook!

651
00:40:04,778 --> 00:40:07,831
I'm still not that good.

652
00:40:07,855 --> 00:40:14,666
Did you cook for your friend yesterday?

653
00:40:14,689 --> 00:40:20,135
I made curry for my friend when they came over.

654
00:40:20,159 --> 00:40:24,032
What did they say?

655
00:40:24,055 --> 00:40:28,588
They said it was delicious and ate a lot.

656
00:40:28,611 --> 00:40:30,978
That's great!

657
00:40:31,001 --> 00:40:35,434
My friend gave me some sweets in return.

658
00:40:35,457 --> 00:40:38,149
What kind of sweets?

659
00:40:38,173 --> 00:40:40,973
They're French pastries.

660
00:40:40,996 --> 00:40:45,529
Sweet treats always cheer you up, don't they?

661
00:40:45,552 --> 00:40:48,885
They're great when you're feeling tired.

662
00:40:48,908 --> 00:40:54,675
I want to cook for my sister too.

663
00:40:54,698 --> 00:40:58,631
Let's eat together when she visits.

664
00:40:58,654 --> 00:41:00,191
Thanks!

665
00:41:00,215 --> 00:41:02,748
She'll be so happy.